  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably mild through the week with a  \nchance of showers Wednesday night into Thursday.\n \nAn expansive area of offshore high pressure will dominate the \nweather through mid-week, delivering an unseasonably warm and\nspring-like stretch of early November weather. Clockwise winds \naround the high will support warm air advection, temperatures \nclimbing 5-10 degrees above the seasonal norm...highs in the 70s \nwith some Piedmont locations approaching 80 by Wednesday. \nDewpoints will also be on the rise with readings in the 50s to \nlower 60s and supporting mild overnight temperatures as well. In\ngeneral, conditions will feel notably pleasant if you like \nwarmth instead of cool and crisp. \n\nAs for rain chances, Low pressure will move through the Upper  \nMidwest and into the Great Lakes Region by Thursday, with the \naccompanying surface front bringing a chance of rain showers to \nthe area Wednesday night and Thursday. Models have continued to \nback off on precipitation coverage, QPF trending lower. From \nwhat we are seeing, the best chance for showers will be along \nand west of the Blue Ridge (amounts 0.25 to 0.50), moisture \nalong the front thinning as it crosses the mountains and \nleaving areas east of the Blue Ridge with less than a quarter of \nan inch of wetting. \n\nMay see some lingering upslope showers along the western slopes \nthrough Saturday given persistent NW flow. Otherwise, quiet \nweather once again returns through the remainder of the week.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Weekend Reset: Cooler, seasonable air returns \nthis weekend.\n\nThursday's frontal passage will begin transition to lower \ntemperatures for the weekend, readings closer to normal for  \nSaturday and Sunday. \n\nModels are advertising a clipper-like system to barrel through \nthe region late Sunday or Monday...this feature originating \nfrom the northern stream and cooler northern latitudes. \nDepending on its track it may draw down temperatures even \nfurther for Monday and Tuesday, suggesting a few days of cooler\nthan normal weather, a taste of what November should be like...\ncool and crisp.",
